'\" t
.nh
.TH "glab" "1" "Sep 2026" "Auto generated by spf13/cobra" ""

.SH "نام (NAME)"
glab-dependency-firewall-ci-summary \- Summarize Dependency Firewall activity from the CI log. (EXPERIMENTAL)


.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBglab dependency-firewall ci-summary [flags]\fP


.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Read \fB\&.gitlab/df/ci-log.json\fR and print blocked and flagged packages
recorded during a \fBglab dependency-firewall\fR run.

.PP
The log is read from the current working directory. Run this command from
the same directory as the \fBglab dependency-firewall\fR run that wrote the
log, otherwise no activity is reported.

.TS
allbox;
l l 
l l .
\fBExit code\fP	\fBMeaning\fP
\fB0\fR	T{
No blocked entries in the log (allow-only or warnings).
T}
\fB1\fR	The log could not be read.
\fB3\fR	T{
At least one entry in the log is blocked.
T}
.TE

.PP
This feature is an experiment and is not ready for production use.
It might be unstable or removed at any time.
For more information, see
https://docs.gitlab.com/policy/development_stages_support/.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	Show help for this command.


.SH "مثال (EXAMPLE)"
.EX
# Show blocked and flagged packages from the last firewall run
glab dependency-firewall ci-summary

.EE


.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBglab-dependency-firewall(1)\fP
